msgid "dlg.help.title"
msgstr "Quick guide"

msgid "dlg.help.body"
msgstr "Managing the gamemode.ini file with privileges.\\n\\nThis application manages the GameMode configuration file. The [gpu] options are applied by the daemon only when the file resides at /etc/gamemode.ini (privileged path): when you enable GPU options, you will be asked for the administrator password via pkexec.\\n\\nGameMode reads multiple files in this order: /usr/share/gamemode/gamemode.ini (provided by the package), /etc/gamemode.ini, ~/.config/gamemode.ini and $PWD/gamemode.ini. Values from later files override earlier ones. This GUI writes to /etc/gamemode.ini, the location intended for the administrator's configuration (and one of the two, together with /usr/share, where the [gpu] section takes effect).\\n\\nTo use renice and core parking you must belong to the 'gamemode' group."

